    "0.0.3": {
        "info": {
            "author": "Manish Sharma",
            "author_email": "manish.sharma@docsumo.com",
            "bugtrack_url": null,
            "classifiers": [
                "Development Status :: 4 - Beta",
                "Intended Audience :: Developers",
                "License :: OSI Approved :: MIT License",
                "Operating System :: OS Independent",
                "Programming Language :: Python :: 3",
                "Topic :: Internet",
                "Topic :: Software Development :: Libraries",
                "Topic :: Software Development :: Libraries :: Python Modules",
                "Topic :: Utilities"
            ],
            "description": "### Fake data Generator Library\n---\n### Description\n- This library intends to generate Fake Information based on the keys provided and count associated with them\n- You can generate \"n\" number of information using this library\n- This library internally uses `Faker` and `Phone-gen` library\n---\n### Usage \n1 : Install the requirements library\n: [Faker](https://pypi.org/project/Faker/) and [phone-gen](https://pypi.org/project/phone-gen/)\n\n2 : Import the library\n```\nfrom fake_info_generation import main\n```\n\n3 : Call the function module\n```\nmain.generate_data_info(name_count=3, zip_count=3, address_count=3, region='IN')\n```\n\n4 : Response [ This response might change due to random generation ]\n```\n{   'Address': [   '4711 Michael Canyon Suite 195\\nGordonport, NV 01575',\n                   '73989 Candace Course\\nSouth Brian, ME 01819',\n                   'Unit 7929 Box 8142\\nDPO AA 71863'],\n    'Name': ['Taylor Lopez', 'Margaret Patrick', 'Jessica Henry'],\n    'Occupation': ['Engineering geologist'],\n    'PhoneNumber': ['7989441126'],\n    'SSN_or_EIN': ['927641785'],\n    'State': ['Iowa'],\n    'Transaction_Value': ['2924'],\n    'ZIP_or_POSTAL': ['21834', '55542', '37100']\n}\n```\n---\n### Default Values\n- By default, all the count params are set to count = 1 \n- Region = \"US\"\n- Trans_range = [1,6]\n- Signed_Num = \"False\"\n----\n\n### Optional Arguments \n- -h, --help :: show this help message and exit\n- --name_count NAME :: Number of names to generate\n- --address_count ADDRESS :: Number of addresses to generate\n- --phone_count PHONE :: Number of phone numbers to generate\n- --zip_count ZIP :: Number of zip codes to generate\n- --state_count STATE :: Number of states to generate\n- --region_count REGION :: Region based on which phone-num is generated\n- --occupation_count OCCUPATION :: Number of occupations to generate\n- --trans_count TRANS_COUNT :: Number of Transaction Values to generate\n- --trans_range TRANS_RANGE [TRANS_RANGE ...] :: The character length range upto which transaction values can be generated. Use [start, end] structure\n- --signed_num SIGNED_NUM :: If set to \"true\", the number can be both positive and negative randomly. Default=False, only positive number\n- --ssn_or_ein_count SSN_OR_EIN :: Number of occupations to generate Social Security Number or Employment Identification Number\n---\n\n",
            "description_content_type": "text/markdown",
